
:: 8/31/2026 MVP actual ytODO

-understanding frame/state semanics
    -frame n is a frame with a completely resolved state
    -frame n* is is a frame with a partially resolved state, when fully resolved will become frame n+1
    -level editor is frame "0*", and game starts at frame 1
    -level editor actually allows showing both frame 0* and frame 1....  frame 1 is just a fake preview. when editing blocks, they must always show frame 0*
    -if resolving to frame 1 pushes block movement onto the state update queue, stop the solver and display an error. the level is invalid and there is no frame 1 preview.

-add support for "Floor" and "level size"
    -floor tiles aren't anything special game logic wise but tehy get special treatement in the editor
    -floor tiles, just regular tiles but maybe the look different (or maybe they just look like regular wall tiles)
    -first make surr you can walk on top of tiles in general, well that should be a property of it, can walk on top property. THis property is actually a perf fact property... mirrors for example have 2 faces that can be walked on!
    -floorplan pop up menu, lets you set a certain Z level filled with floor b0locks (default z=-1) up to some level size (w,h)... 0,0 is still bottom left corner
        -you may need to update the default level to move the floor blocks down to z =-1
    -add a "lock floor" button which takes a z level (auto set by the floorplan popup) and makes all blocks on that level not selectable.

-improve selection
    -create selection mode
    -in both placement modes, alllow shift click to select multiple blocks
    -in z layer placement mode, allow lcick + drag to multi select. clicknig on a block + dragging prioritizes box selection rather than move block
        -in raycast placement mode, no box seleciton, click + dragging on a block moves it
    -create a button that says "combine" that combines all block in a selection into 1 mega block IF all the blocks are moveable, (button is greyed out if they are not)

-make level editor window resizeable if not already

-create glass block (moveable/immoveable) transparent block that laser just passes through.


-improve visual language for testing
    -sharp corner block = immovable
    -rounded corner block = pushable
    -so we need botha sharp and round corner variant of mirror and laser and regular block
    -in general moveable objects are brighter in color as well.
    -for now, we have only the following blocks to support, so this will bethe set we mainly experiment with for our MVP
        -block, moveable/immovable (can be walked on)
        -glass block, moveable/immoveable (can be walked on)
        -mirror, moveable/immoveable (2 surfaces can be walked on)
        -laser, moveable/immovabel (only laser surface can't be walked on)
        -goal block, moveable/immovable (no surface can be walked on)




